# Generated corpora, indexes, and models are not committed. The labeled query
# set is evidence rather than output, so it lives in braid/eval/queryset/ and is
# committed with the code.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
# The manifest is committed: it carries the seed, the counts, and the frozen
# corpus_hash that Checkpoint B audits. The corpus itself is regenerable from
# it, so the corpus stays out.
!data/manifest.json
# The extraction-quality sample and its hand annotations are evidence, the
# same reasoning as the query set: Task 21's own Verify step requires the
# report's numbers to "regenerate from the committed annotations", which is
# impossible if these are gitignored. triples.jsonl itself stays out -- it is
# large (thousands of lines) and deterministically regenerable from the
# corpus and code, unlike the hand annotations.
!data/extract-sample.jsonl
!data/extract-gold.jsonl
!data/extract-manifest.json
models/
reports/*.png
# Stub-run output is placeholder data proving the harness runs end to end,
# not evidence. reports/*.md otherwise stays tracked -- extraction-quality.md,
# finetune.md, comparison.md (the real run), graph-vs-vector.md are evidence.
reports/stub-*.md

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
